      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm here to help you explore this further. It's understandable to feel concerned and want to uncover the truth about your childhood. Public archives can be a good starting point, as they may hold records such as birth and adoption documents, school records, and other public records that could shed some light on your past. You can also try researching local libraries, particularly those with historical societies or special collections, as they may have access to more specific records or newspaper archives from the area where you were living. Additionally, you may want to consider reaching out to local government offices, as they may have records related to your birth or residency.",
